MacPhoenix's changes to Executor, and its CPU glue: MIT

MacPhoenix as a whole is distributed under the GNU GPL, version 2, because
it links GPL code (the UAE 68k core, SheepShaver's PowerPC machine). The
files listed below don't depend on that code, and their MacPhoenix
authorship is additionally licensed under the MIT licence below, so they
can go back into Executor (https://github.com/autc04/executor) or anywhere
else on Executor's own terms.

Covered (the MacPhoenix changes and additions in):

  src/executor/            everything, including romlib/, multiversal/,
                           cpu/ (the syn68k facade, PowerCore on mame-ppc),
                           host/ and tests/; third_party/ keeps its own
                           licences
  src/cpu/core/            the cpu::Core interface and its glue, except
                           uae_core.cpp (glue to the GPL UAE core)
  src/cpu/mame/            mame_68k_core.cpp, mame_ppc_core.cpp and shim/
                           (MacPhoenix's stand-in for MAME's framework)

Not covered: the MAME CPU cores themselves (src/cpu/mame/m68000, powerpc,
cpu, emu, and the MAME utility headers lifted into shim/) are MAME's, under
BSD-3-Clause (src/cpu/mame/LICENSE-MAME, and each file's header); asmjit is
under the zlib licence (src/cpu/mame/LICENSE-asmjit). Executor's own code
stays under its MIT licence (COPYING). The whole repository's licensing:
LICENSING.md at the top; what MacPhoenix changed in Executor:
docs/executor/README.md.

